  <h2>What is Polki?</h2>
  <p>Polki refers to uncut diamonds set in gold. Instead of the many facets of a modern brilliant cut, Polki stones keep a flatter, natural form, which gives a warm, candle-like shine rather than sharp sparkle. The style traces back to royal Rajasthani and Mughal courts.</p>

  <h2>Polki at Vaishnavi Jewels</h2>
  <p>We make Polki chokers, long necklaces, full bridal sets, earrings, maang tikkas and bangles, often combined with emeralds, rubies and pearls. Many of our Polki pieces are set in the <a href="/jadau-jewellery">Jadau</a> technique.</p>

  <h2>Customisation</h2>
  <p>Designs can be adjusted in size, stone colours and layout to suit your outfit and occasion. Visit the showroom or book a video call to see pieces up close.</p>

  <p>Read more: <a href="/blog/polki-vs-jadau-guide">Polki vs Jadau &ndash; what's the difference?</a></p>
